Package: bruce
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Urban Climate Estimation from Heterogeneous Station Networks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ayrton", "Gouveia", email = "ayrtonsgouveia19@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Spatiotemporal interpolation of daily urban air temperature by
    fusing observation networks of different quality (official stations,
    airports, low-cost IoT sensors, citizen weather stations) with an optional
    gridded background product such as a reanalysis. Each network enters with
    its own Gaussian likelihood; networks declared as biased receive a fixed
    offset and station-level random effects, and a Matern SPDE field evolving
    day to day through an AR(1) structure captures the residual spatial signal.
    Fitting uses R-INLA. The package also provides leave-station-out and
    leave-region-out cross-validation with CRPS, detection of degenerate fits,
    posterior prediction on a raster grid, zonal aggregation and a simulator
    for synthetic cities. City-agnostic by design: all city-specific inputs
    are declared through a small data contract.
